-- M1c: the sharper question M1 raises. M1 showed two impls differing only in an
-- effect row are REJECTED as overlapping (coherence strips the effect too), so
-- the ppTy fold is vacuous for the two-impl case.
--
-- But a SINGLE effect-carrying impl has no overlap to be rejected for. If it is
-- accepted, then today eval mints "Sz|Int|" (ppTyK strips TyEffect) while the
-- typechecker stamps "Sz|<Stdout> Int|" (ppTy renders it) -- a caller-side word
-- that NO definition-side entry carries. That is the skew keyForSite's header
-- warns is "silent on the direct-call path and live on the RDict path", and it
-- would exist TODAY, before bite e.
interface Sz a where
  sz : a -> Int

impl Sz (<Stdout> Int) where
  sz _ = 2

main = println (sz 0)
